{"id":"NCT07361510","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy of Pumitamig Versus Pembrolizumab in Participants With Previously Untreated Advanced Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer and PD-L1 ≥ 50%. (ROSETTA Lung-202)","official":"ROSETTA Lung-202: A Randomized, Double-Blind, Phase 3 Study of Pumitamig Monotherapy Compared to Pembrolizumab as First-line Treatment in Participants With Locally Advanced or Metastatic Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer With PD-L1 ≥ 50%.","summary":"The purpose of this study is to evaluate the efficacy of Pumitamig versus Pembrolizumab in participants with previously untreated advanced Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer and PD-L1 ≥ 50%.","conditions":["Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Pumitamig"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Pembrolizumab"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria\n\n* Participants must have a histologically or cytologically confirmed diagnosis of Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC) (squamous and nonsquamous) with Stage IIIB/IIIC or Stage IV disease.\n* Participants must have a programmed death ligand-1 (PD-L1) expression ≥ 50%.\n* Participants must have measurable disease as defined by Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) v1.1.\n* Participants must have no prior systemic anti-tumor therapy for locally advanced or metastatic NSCLC.\n* Participants must have an Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) Performance Status 0-1.\n\nExclusion Criteria\n\n* Participants must not have any documented actionable genomic alteration (AGA) for which first-line (1L) approved therapies are indicated.\n* Participants must not have any symptomatic untreated central nervous system (CNS) metastases, leptomeningeal metastases (carcinomatous meningitis) or spinal cord compression.\n* Participants must not have any significant cardiovascular impairment as evidenced by uncontrolled hypertension (despite optimal medical treatment), congestive heart failure, active coronary disease (within 6 months prior to randomization), ventricular arrhythmias, or major thrombotic or embolic events or major hemorrhagic events (within 6 months prior to randomization), or significant risk of pulmonary hemorrhage.\n* Participants must not an active autoimmune disease.\n* Other protocol-defined Inclusion/Exclusion criteria apply.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":750,"start":"2026-03-12","pcd":"2031-10-14","upd":"2026-10-23","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","areas":["oncology","rare"],"central":["BMS Clinical Trials Contact Center www.BMSClinicalTrials.com · 855-907-3286 · Clinical.Trials@bms.com","First line of the email MUST contain NCT # and Site #."],"sites":[{"f":"Southern Cancer Center Pc","city":"Daphne","pr":"Alabama","zip":"36526","s":"R","lat":30.6035,"lon":-87.9036,"c":"Michael Meshad, Site 0348 · 111-111-1111"},{"f":"Mohtaseb Cancer Center & Blood Disorders","city":"Bullhead City","pr":"Arizona","zip":"86442","s":"R","lat":35.1478,"lon":-114.5683,"c":"Hamdy Mohtaseb, Site 0424"},{"f":"Palo Verde Hematology Oncology","city":"Glendale","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85304","s":"R","lat":33.5386,"lon":-112.186,"c":"Amol Rakkar, Site 0391 · 602-978-6255"},{"f":"Beverly Hills Cancer Center","city":"Beverly Hills","pr":"California","zip":"90211","s":"R","lat":34.0736,"lon":-118.4004,"c":"Afshin Gabayan, Site 0352 · 310-432-8955"},{"f":"Orange Coast Memorial Medical Center","city":"Fountain Valley","pr":"California","zip":"92708","s":"R","lat":33.7092,"lon":-117.9537,"c":"Amol Rao, Site 0299 · 510673-1293"},{"f":"Cancer and Blood Specialty Clinic","city":"Los Alamitos","pr":"California","zip":"90720","s":"R","lat":33.8031,"lon":-118.0726,"c":"Nihal Abdulla, Site 0027 · 562-706-6648"},{"f":"UCLA","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90095","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Edward Garon, Site 0422 · 310-926-5333"},{"f":"Pacific Cancer Care","city":"Monterey","pr":"California","zip":"93940","s":"R","la